          "python",
          "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n\n# Create pipeline\npipe = Pipeline([\n    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n\n### Handling Expensive Model Evaluation\n\nSome models are computationally expensive to evaluate (neural networks with large datasets). Strategies:\n\n**Approximate evaluation**: Use subset of training data for CV folds. Saves computation but introduces higher variance in CV scores.\n\n**Parallelization**: n_jobs=-1 in sklearn evaluates multiple configurations in parallel, scaling linearly with processor count.\n\n**Early termination**: For iterative algorithms, halt after few epochs if showing promise vs stopping at max_iter.\n    ('classifier', RandomForestClassifier())\n])\n\n# Define parameter grid\nparam_grid = {\n    'classifier__n_estimators': [50, 100, 200],\n    'classifier__max_depth': [5, 10, 15],\n    'classifier__min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10]\n}\n\n# Grid search\ngrid = GridSearchCV(pipe, param_grid, cv=5, n_jobs=-1)\ngrid.fit(X_train, y_train)"
